WEBVTT

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.660
Front wedgie! Front wedgie! Front wedgie!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.790
Stop! Now I'm picturing it!

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.160
Azu, you pervert!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.370
Huh?!

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.950
We're in the air. Now commencing the plan.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.080
I can't be a bride anymore!

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.940
6 hours before 
swimsuit takeoff

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.450
Episode 4
 Tateyama Castle Swimsuit Skirmish!

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.450
Episode 4
 Tateyama Castle Swimsuit Skirmish!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.200
Here goes! Hero Cannon...

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.370
...fire!

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.700
I hit it, but it won't stay dead!

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:47.120
We only have so much fuel.
At this rate, the city will be in trouble!

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.410
This sound...

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.740
Azu, Azu! Do something!

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:57.120
Shuddap! This noise is driving me nuts!
Gimme a second to think--

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.370
I'm hit!

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.620
Komagome is hit! She can't continue flying!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.790
The city is empty and
clear for emergency landing.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.540
Stop

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.330
Find somewhere to land!

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.790
Gear down!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:20.160
Calculating landing area. Route 257, Point C3.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.540
Position reached!

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.290
Landing... now!

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:36.370
Komagome's okay. Status?

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:41.240
Unknown. I managed to take one down, but...

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.910
It keeps reviving. No progress.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.200
There's just no end to them!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.200
Plus, the radio won't shut up,
and I can't take it!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.870
We can't win without more info.
Keep the battle going till it's out of juice!

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.040
Azu? Get to safety!

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.450
How about you guys work together
and end this instead?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.080
Right. Command, how long are they active?

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.120
For 1400 seconds.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.790
That's just 120 more.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:11.310
Roger!

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:11.790
Oof!

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.860
We've got this!

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.490
Ow, ow, ow...

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.290
Huh?

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.370
Yikes!

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:42.370
Azu! Azu! Wake up, Azu!

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.790
Shuddap! Five more minutes!

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.870
That's so cliché.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.410
Azu, you got knocked out!
Don't you remember?

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:54.660
Knocked out? Knocked out, huh?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.160
It happened to <i>me</i> ?!

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:01.410
That's right! We were so worried!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.410
I'm suffocating, idiot! Let go!

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.740
Didn't you hear me, idiot?!
What happened to the Pillar?!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.790
Like Azuzu suggested,
we wore it out until it stopped.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.410
But that only buys us some time.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.490
Good girl! Good girl!

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:14.830
I see.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.950
There's a lot to do before it comes back.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.620
Hero Wing repair,
figuring out where it'll show...

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.830
Assessing your physical health...
That's number one.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.330
Azu hasn't been sleeping.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.330
Erk!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.790
And that's why you fell over.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:37.870
Given our divine protection,
we should rarely collapse to a Pillar's effects.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.370
Yeah! Azu pushes herself too hard!

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.910
So...! Eat this!

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.080
Where did all this come from?!

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.290
Thanks for the meal!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.830
Eat! Sleep! Recover!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.620
My body's a little more complicated.
It's not like yours.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:02.200
But... Miyako brings up... a good point.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.910
You can't fight on an empty stomach!

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:10.490
Argh, sheesh! Everyone's mind
was poisoned by the idiot!

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.240
Jeez, you're so stubborn!

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.790
Huh? What are you...?

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.660
Here you are! Thank you for your service!

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:27.240
m 0 0 l 332 0 l 332 80 l 0 80

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:27.240
Soup Kitchen

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.240
Thank you!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:34.740
The city people made everyone food.
Won't you eat?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.290
Fine! But I'm taking out the stuff I hate!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.040
Only the plate will be left.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:50.040
So, who's gonna tell me
what happened while I was out?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:50.990
Me! Me! Me!

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.120
Shut up, idiot.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.370
Azu!

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.370
Me.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:55.200
Hmm?

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.990
Maintenance is quickly servicing our planes.

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:03.700
Also, control noticed the Pillar
emits strange sound waves.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.740
Sound waves?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.910
They're trying to analyze the pattern.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:12.410
We're hoping it matches
a Pillar we've battled before.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.450
That's a long shot.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.080
Azu...

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.540
You're so annoying! Just say it!

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.660
Uh, I don't know what their deal is, but...

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.490
But?

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.240
There's kids.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.160
I think they want something.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.830
Weren't you brats just--

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.040
You'll scare them making that face.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.910
Is there something we can help with?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.040
Um...

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.830
If something's the matter, please say.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:08:00.990
We're soldiers. We want to help
civilians like you as much as possible.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.450
Um, look!

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:06.450
Huh?

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:07.410
A phone?

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.790
Huh? Is that us?

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:12.080
What are we supposed to see?

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.660
Just watch!

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.040
Yeah! They got one!

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.450
What's that sound?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.160
That buzzing?

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:25.040
Huh, it's back? That was weird.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.830
You hear that again?

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.740
That one came back too!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.490
Huh? Someone got hit! They're falling this way!

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.330
Whoa!

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.160
Azu, don't get all depressed.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.790
Wanna practice more?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.290
I'll help.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.290
Good work.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.580
Azu, you had an idea?

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:00.490
You can tell?

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:05.410
I can! The face you're making
is my favorite one!

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.540
What did you figure out?

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.450
How to outwit the Pillars
and rub it in their faces!

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.450
Faces?

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.660
Do Pillars have faces?

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.620
Huh? You know what the sound wave is?

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:22.080
That's Komagome for you. Always pulls through.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.700
They're using ultrasonic frequencies
that most people can't hear.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:30.450
Ultrasonic frequencies? A mosquito tone?

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:32.410
A what?

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:37.830
It's a high-pitched sound.
It's like a mosquito buzzing by your ear.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.790
Oh! That buzzing sound!

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.660
Yeah. When a Pillar is destroyed,

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:47.120
it emits a sound signaling
another Pillar to regenerate it.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:52.540
By the way, you can't hear it if you're too old.
Only young people can.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.990
That explains a lot.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.490
I-I swear I heard it! I heard it, okay?!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:08.290
Anyways, if we know the signal,
we can disrupt it.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.080
If we do that while we attack...

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.950
Huh? Hey, what's going on?

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.410
Um, don't panic when you see this.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.660
Is that Tateyama Castle by the base?

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.870
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:25.950
Go figure.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:30.490
Yeah. It reappeared right outside the base.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:35.450
Getting you back to your
Hero Wings will be a problem.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.540
Tell us the whole situation.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.990
Four Tertiary Pillars appeared in Tateyama.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:46.240
Their search range extends to 2,000 meters.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:48.290
But for some unknown reason,

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:53.620
one moved near Tateyama Castle
and expanded the range.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.660
And... why can't we return to base?

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:02.240
Because Pillars have a preference
when choosing targets.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.990
For weapons, they attack planes first.
But as for people...

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.990
They go after Valkyrie.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:12.830
So the moment we step into their range,
they'll attack right away.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:14.370
I see.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:21.410
We asked help from other bases,
but everyone's afraid of Pillars appearing.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:24.160
How long till the nearest one is active?

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.580
Roughly 90 minutes.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:31.830
There you have it. We need you back
before then to get in the air.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.290
I see.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:37.910
What if we sneaked back or sped home in a car?

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:42.870
We've tried that with Valkyries
in the past, but we don't anymore.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.540
Guess how it went.

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.910
I see.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:50.120
But how do Pillars even know that it's us?

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:54.620
They can tell. While some use hearing and sight,

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:58.490
others can sense our divine protection.

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:02.080
These ones use high frequencies to detect us.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:05.540
But people have avoided detection underground.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:06.870
Underground?

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.740
We overheard everything!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.490
Mysterious Pillar by the castle...

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:17.830
You're kinda in our way!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:21.080
No matter what, we're coming through!

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:24.450
If you can't beat it, push past it!

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:28.870
We know a way to get our Valkyries home! Cheese!

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:31.330
Too much!

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.940
If you really know a way...

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:34.740
We do!

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:35.530
Huh?

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:36.410
So tight.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:37.280
Do you?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:37.990
We do!

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:41.700
But you'll all have to be ready to work hard!

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:42.280
Cheese!

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.160
Too much!

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:43.700
Huh?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:44.790
Of course!

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.990
We're always working our hardest!

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:50.160
That's our Miko for you! Atta girl!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.120
Cheese!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.490
What's your plan?

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.910
Well...

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:54.910
It's simple!

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:55.840
Simple?!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:56.540
So tight!

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:00.580
It's what seduced us to come to this base!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.120
And that's...!

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.240
That's... the sea!

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.660
You know it! The sea!

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.910
If nothing else, the sea!

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:16.370
Clappity clap! It's our sea!

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:21.870
"Big Catch"

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.200
The sea!

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.870
Too much!

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.240
Sigururi!

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.700
Sigururi.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:36.550
80 minutes before 
swimsuit takeoff

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:37.370
Before the Pillars awaken,
we need to get you airborne. Therefore!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:42.040
We leave Taibusa-Misaki by sea
and stay out of their search range.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:46.410
Using an underground path,
we'll guide you back to base.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:46.410
Your head's in the way! Your head!

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:47.620
Somehow or another!

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.620
Somehow or another?

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.950
So, any questions?

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:55.160
First of all, why the <i>fundoshi</i> ?

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.200
That's...

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.200
...because...

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.160
...Japanese people...

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.330
...put appearances first!

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:06.790
Well, why the hell are we in swimsuits?!

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:09.870
Clap, clap, clappity, clappity clap, clap!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.490
That was too fast! Again! Go!

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:20.080
Clap, clap, clap! Clappity clap!

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.990
Clap, clap, clap! Clap!

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:24.240
You're all so cute!

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.740
At the sea...

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:31.790
You've gotta wear swimsuits!
Swimsuits... Swimsuits... Swimsuits...

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.740
Yeah!

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:38.910
What the...?!

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:39.990
Argh! It reeks of sweat!

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:39.990
Listen up.

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.450
This is a stealth mission!

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:43.870
Therefore...

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.030
"Big Catch"

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:48.870
Let's do our best not to stand out!

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:55.080
It's cramped and reeks of sweat!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.790
Ugh! That was too much to handle.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:03.040
65 minutes before 
swimsuit takeoff

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:02.450
This leads to the base?

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:06.540
That's right! And don't worry,
it's quite nice inside!

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.990
It'll feel like you're at a resort!

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:14.580
We poured our hearts into making
this should it ever be needed!

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.040
60 minutes before
 swimsuit takeoff

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:21.580
It'll feel like a resort?

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:26.490
The Pillar's effects will get even stronger.
Everyone, be careful!

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:27.080
Yeah!

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.950
Guys! Pay attention to what Claudy says!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.950
And what Miko says too!

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.540
Yeah! Obviously!

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:37.830
Rest assured. We're full
of spirit and ready to ro--

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.160
55 minutes before
 swimsuit takeoff

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:41.370
Pretty Boy! Pretty Boy...
Pretty Boy... Pretty Boy...

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.910
It'll feel like a resort?

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:47.740
Well, this is certainly
an adventurous date spot.

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:50.080
Who would come here for a date?!

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.040
But it <i>is</i> titillating!

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.910
Having said that,
it shouldn't be this dangerous.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.790
Must be the Pillar's influence.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.870
Huh? Didn't you just fall?

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:03.080
More importantly, we need to focus
on getting out of here before--

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:06.040
Pretty Boy! Pretty Boy... Pretty Boy...

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:09.040
Dammit! We shall get revenge!

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.040
Clappity...

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:10.700
Clap!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.450
Don't you join in!

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:16.040
40 minutes before
swimsuit takeoff

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.490
Pretty Boy!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:17.910
It's no fair!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.790
Don't take all the good parts!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.450
Didn't you just fall?

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.450
Come on! Have courage! Use me as a bridge!

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.120
Hurry!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.700
Okay.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:33.370
Here goes...

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:38.450
Right now, I'm being helpful to Sonoka! I am!

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:44.080
I won't look up! I won't!
I'm fine just being helpful to her!

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:45.450
Whoops! Sorry!

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.830
Pretty Boy!

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:56.330
Pretty Boy may die, but my favorite lives on.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:58.330
Pretty Boy!

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.700
Dammit!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.540
We'll help too!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.870
35 minutes before 
swimsuit takeoff

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.910
It's time for us to shine!

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:11.160
Let's show 'em the pillar of manhood!

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.410
The pillar of manhood!

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:17.770
"Pillar of Manhood"

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.830
Wh-Whoa! Too much!

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:24.830
Come on and cross!
We're risking our lives for this bridge!

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.830
15 minutes before
 swimsuit takeoff

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.620
--Good luck!
--How'd you get across?!

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:31.200
--The Pillars will be active
any minute now! Just go for it!
--You just fell!
--Help out already!

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.700
But it's too much!

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.660
Then I'll go first!

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:46.950
This very moment, I'm being helpful to Miko.

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:52.490
I'm proving useful to her!
I won't look behind! I won't!

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:58.580
All I care about is being
helpful to Miko! That's it!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.040
Where is she?

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.830
Huh? Where'd she go?

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:08.790
Ack! How?! When did she...?!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:13.040
Dammit! I was skipped!
It feels like my scene got cut!

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.990
Sorry! Coming through!

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:19.700
Dammit! I wanted Miko to step on me too!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:19.700
